  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shell"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "shell"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " border makes the square look finished without a separate edging step — the scalloped shape of five trebles per corner and three trebles per side position sits naturally as a final design element rather than an afterthought. Rounds 1 to 3 are the standard granny structure with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-cluster"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble clusters"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Round 4 replaces each cluster position with a shell worked directly into the chain spaces from round 3. Start from a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " fans out the border shells to their full width."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK cotton, approx 35 m per square. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "11 × 11 cm in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook. The shell border adds a small amount of width over a standard four-round granny — check at round 3: target 8 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3-treble cluster (3tr cl)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Shell: 5 tr in corner sp; 3 tr in side ch-1 sp"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 at the start of rounds 1 to 3 counts as the first tr. Round 4 is the shell border — ch 3 at the start counts as the first tr of the first shell."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 2 tr, ch 2. *(3 tr, ch 2); repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. Pull tail. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corners)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 4 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in ch-1 sp on side. Ch 1. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. 3 tr in last side sp. Ch 1. Sl st to top of ch-3. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 8 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4 — shell border"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner ch-2 sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 4 tr in same corner sp (first corner shell of 5 tr). *3 tr in each ch-1 side sp across side (side shell of 3 tr per sp). 5 tr in next corner ch-2 sp (corner shell); repeat from * 2 more times. 3 tr in each remaining side sp. Sl st to top of ch-3. Fasten off. (4 corner shells of 5 tr, 8 side shells of 3 tr) = (20 tr corner + 24 tr side) = (44 tr)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chart"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "roundCount": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Wet-block to 11 × 11 cm, pinning the outer tips of the corner shells to sharpen the shell fan shape. The scalloped border needs pinning to sit evenly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join shell-border squares by working through the tops of the outer shell trebles. Lay two squares wrong sides together and slip stitch through the 3rd (centre) treble of each side shell in turn. At the corner, join through the 3rd treble of each corner shell."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 degrees on a gentle cycle. The shell border may close slightly after washing — a light re-block with a damp cloth and pinning will reopen the fans."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work the shell border in a contrast colour for a clear two-tone shell edge. Or increase the corner shell to 7 trebles (instead of 5) and the side shells to 5 trebles for a more pronounced scallop."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}